% c296 (playability; Adler ch. 4, adler1 PDF 114-115: "Chords may be arpeggiated or played solidly"; "Three-note chords (per hand) spread wide are the most effective", tenths are easy (Ex. IV-5);
%   Ex. IV-7, Brahms Requiem i 150-58: the harp's broken chords end in plucked solid chords at the cadence; PDF 113: the middle two octaves are "very rich and warm"): the harp's G-area crescendo (129-130)
